**What’s happening**

1. **`map.loadImage` no longer accepts a callback** – starting with **MapLibre GL v4.0.0** the method returns a **Promise** instead of invoking a callback you pass.  
2. Because the promise is never awaited, the image never gets added, so any style that refers to the image (`icon-image: 'pin'`) ends up with a missing-icon and you see the “callback not being called” warning.

**Fix it in two easy steps**

| Step | What to do | Why it matters |
|------|------------|----------------|
| **1️⃣ Convert the callback to a promise** | ```js<br>// old Mapbox style (won’t work in MapLibre v4+)<br>map.loadImage(url, (err, img) => { … });<br><br>// new MapLibre style (async/await or .then)<br>async function addPin(url) {<br>  try {<br>    const { data: img } = await map.loadImage(url); // ← returns a promise<br>    map.addImage('pin', img);<br>  } catch (err) {<br>    console.error('Failed to load pin image', err);\n>    // you can still throw if you want the app to stop\n>    throw err;\n>  }<br>}<br><br>// call it after the map is ready (see step 2)\n>addPin('https://example.com/pin.png');``` | The promise resolves with an object `{data: ImageBitmap}` (or `{data: HTMLImageElement}` in older browsers). Using `await` (or `.then`) guarantees the image is loaded **before** you call `addImage`. |
| **2️⃣ Add the image *after* the map is fully loaded** | ```js<br>map.on('load', () => {<br>  // the map’s style is now ready – you can safely add custom images<br>  addPin('https://example.com/pin.png');<br>});``` | If you call `addImage` before the `load` event, the style’s sprite isn’t ready yet and the image gets ignored. The `load` event is the same place you’d have called `map.loadImage` in a Mapbox app. |

