### What’s happening?

`map.loadImage` changed in **MapLibre GL v4.0.0** (and later) :

| Mapbox GL JS (≤ v3) | MapLibre GL v4+ |
|--------------------|----------------|
| `map.loadImage(url, callback)` – **callback** is required | **returns a `Promise`** that resolves with `{ data: ImageBitmap }`. The callback signature is no longer accepted, so the function you passed is ignored and the image never gets added to the style. |

Because the image never loads, any style layer that references the image (e.g. `icon-image: 'pin'`) ends up with a missing-icon and you see the “callback not being called” message in the console.

---

## Fix it – use the promise API

### 1️⃣ Simple `.then()` version

```javascript
// old (Mapbox)
map.loadImage(url, (err, img) => {
  if (err) throw err;
  map.addImage('pin', img);
});
```

```javascript
// new (MapLibre)
map.loadImage(url)
  .then(({ data }) => {
    // `data` is an ImageBitmap (or HTMLImageElement in older browsers)
    map.addImage('pin', data);
  })
  .catch(err => {
    // handle loading errors the same way you did before
    console.error('Failed to load marker icon:', err);
    throw err;
  });
```

### 2️⃣ `async/await` version (cleaner if you’re already in an async context)

```javascript
async function addPinIcon(url) {
  try {
    const { data } = await map.loadImage(url);
    map.addImage('pin', data);
  } catch (err) {
    console.error('Failed to load marker icon:', err);
    throw err;
  }
}

// call it after the map is ready
map.on('load', () => addPinIcon('https://example.com/pin.png'));
```

> **Tip:** If you’re loading several icons at once, `Promise.all` is handy:

```javascript
const icons = [
  { name: 'pin',   url: '/icons/pin.png' },
  { name: 'star',  url: '/icons/star.png' },
  // …
];

Promise.all(
  icons.map(i => map.loadImage(i.url).then(({ data }) => ({ name: i.name, data })))
).then(results => {
  results.forEach(({ name, data }) => map.addImage(name, data));
});
```

