## Other places you might still be using callbacks

MapLibre also switched a few other methods from callbacks to promises. If you see similar “callback not called” warnings elsewhere, check these:

| Mapbox method (callback) | MapLibre (promise) |
|--------------------------|--------------------|
| `source.getClusterExpansionZoom(clusterId, cb)` | `source.getClusterExpansionZoom(clusterId)` → returns `Promise<number>` |
| `source.getClusterChildren(clusterId, cb)` | `source.getClusterChildren(clusterId)` → returns `Promise<FeatureCollection>` |
| `source.getClusterLeaves(clusterId, limit, offset, cb)` | `source.getClusterLeaves(clusterId, limit, offset)` → returns `Promise<FeatureCollection>` |
| `map.setRTLTextPlugin(url, cb)` | Returns a `Promise` (and is deprecated from v6.9.0 – Arabic/Hebrew works out-of-the-box) |

Replace those with `await`/`.then()` in the same way.

