## TL;DR

* **`map.loadImage` no longer accepts a callback** – it returns a promise.  
* Convert your code to `await map.loadImage(url)` (or `.then`) and then call `map.addImage`.  
* Once the image is added, any layer that references `'pin'` will show the icon again.

That’s all you need to get your custom marker icons back after swapping to MapLibre GL. 🎉 If you run into any other “missing-icon” or callback-related errors, look for the same pattern (callback → promise) and apply the same fix. Happy mapping!

