```

After swapping to the promise version, the image is added, the `'pin'` symbol resolves, and your markers show up again. 🎉

If you run into any other “missing method” or “blank map” errors, let me know the exact message and the code that triggers it – we can troubleshoot the next piece together.

### What’s happening?

`map.loadImage` changed in **MapLibre GL v4.0.0** (and later).  
- In Mapbox GL JS the method accepted a **callback** (`(err, image) => …`).  
- In MapLibre GL v4+ the method **returns a `Promise`** and **ignores any callback argument**.  

Because the callback is never invoked, your `addImage('pin', img)` never runs, so the sprite you later reference in your marker style (`icon-image: 'pin'`) is missing – the markers appear as blank circles (or disappear completely).

### Fix it – use the promise API

You have three idiomatic ways to handle the promise:

| Style | Code |
|-------|------|
| **`async/await`** (most readable) | ```js\nasync function addPin(url) {\n  const { data: img } = await map.loadImage(url);\n  map.addImage('pin', img);\n}\naddPin('https://example.com/pin.png');\n``` |
| **`.then()`** chain | ```js\nmap.loadImage('https://example.com/pin.png')\n   .then(({ data: img }) => map.addImage('pin', img))\n   .catch(err => { console.error(err); });\n``` |
| **`Promise` with destructuring** (if you already have a promise) | ```js\nconst imgPromise = map.loadImage('https://example.com/pin.png');\nimgPromise.then(res => map.addImage('pin', res.data)).catch(console.error);\n``` |

> **Note:** The resolved value is an object `{ data: HTMLImageElement }`.  
> The older callback used the raw `HTMLImageElement` directly, so you need the `.data` property when using the promise form.

### Full-example (including marker creation)

```js
// 1️⃣  Create the map (already done in your app)
const map = new maplibregl.Map({
  container: 'map',
  style: 'https://tiles.openfreemap.org/styles/liberty', // any non-Mapbox style
  center: [-122.42, 37.78],
  zoom: 12
});

// 2️⃣  Load the icon and add it to the style
async function loadPinIcon() {
  try {
    const { data: img } = await map.loadImage(
      'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/maplibre/maplibre-gl-js/main/docs/assets/pin.png'
    );
    // `addImage` will replace an existing image with the same name if it exists
    map.addImage('pin', img);
  } catch (e) {
    console.error('Failed to load pin image:', e);
  }
}

// 3️⃣  Wait for the style to be ready, then add the image and a marker layer
map.on('style.load', async () => {
  await loadPinIcon();

  // Example: a GeoJSON source with a single point
  map.addSource('my-points', {
    type: 'geojson',
    data: {
      type: 'FeatureCollection',
      features: [
        {
          type: 'Feature',
          geometry: { type: 'Point', coordinates: [-122.42, 37.78] },
          properties: {}
        }
      ]
    }
  });

  // Use the image we just added
  map.addLayer({
    id: 'my-points-layer',
    type: 'symbol',
    source: 'my-points',
    layout: {
      'icon-image': 'pin',
      'icon-size': 0.8,
      'icon-allow-overlap': true
    }
  });
});
```

### Why the marker icons disappear

- **Missing image** – `map.addImage('pin', img)` never ran → the style can’t find `'pin'`.
- **Fallback** – When a symbol layer references a non-existent image, MapLibre draws **no icon** (the feature is still there, you can see it with `queryRenderedFeatures` but it’s invisible).

Once the image is successfully added, the markers will render again.

### Quick checklist for the rest of your migration

| ✅ | Item | What to verify |
|---|------|----------------|
| 1 | **Package & import** | `npm i maplibre-gl` and `import * as maplibregl from 'maplibre-gl';` |
| 2 | **Namespace** | All `mapboxgl` → `maplibregl` (including CSS class prefixes). |
| 3 | **Access token** | Remove any `mapboxgl.accessToken = …` line. |
| 4 | **Style URL** | No `mapbox://…` URLs. Use an open-source style (e.g. OpenFreeMap, MapTiler, your own). |
| 5 | **Callback → Promise** | `loadImage`, `GeoJSONSource` cluster methods, `setRTLTextPlugin`, etc. |
| 6 | **v2-only APIs** | `setFog` → `setSky`; free-camera methods → `calculateCameraOptionsFromCameraLngLatAltRotation` + `jumpTo/easeTo/flyTo`. |
| 7 | **Plugins** | Replace Mapbox-only plugins (`@mapbox/mapbox-gl-geocoder`, `@mapbox/mapbox-gl-directions`) with their MapLibre equivalents (`@maplibre/maplibre-gl-geocoder`, `@maplibre/maplibre-gl-directions`). |
| 8 | **CSS class names** | `mapboxgl-ctrl` → `maplibregl-ctrl`, etc. |
| 9 | **CORS / sprite / glyph URLs** | Ensure any custom style’s `sprite` and `glyphs` URLs point to publicly accessible resources (no `mapbox://`). |

### TL;DR fix for your specific problem

```js
// Old (Mapbox) – does NOT work in MapLibre
map.loadImage(url, (err, img) => {
  if (err) throw err;
  map.addImage('pin', img);
});

// New (MapLibre) – use the promise
