   .then(({ data: img }) => map.addImage('pin', img))
   .catch(err => console.error('loadImage error:', err));
```

After swapping to the promise version, the image will be added, the `'pin'` symbol will be found, and your markers will appear again. 🎉

If you run into any other “callback not called” warnings (e.g., `source.getClusterChildren`, `source.getClusterLeaves`, `source.getClusterExpansionZoom`), apply the same pattern: replace the callback with `await`/`.then()`.

