|10| **Glyphs / sprites** | If you kept a Mapbox style, replace `glyphs` and `sprite` URLs with ones that actually exist for your new source (or host your own). |

### TL;DR for your specific problem

```js
// Old (Mapbox) – callback is ignored in MapLibre
map.loadImage(url, (err, img) => { … });

/* New (MapLibre) – use the promise */
map.loadImage(url)
   .then(({ data: img }) => map.addImage('pin', img))
   .catch(err => console.error(err));
```

After swapping to the promise version, the image is added, the `'pin'` symbol resolves, and your markers show up again. 🎉

