**What’s happening**

1. **`map.loadImage` no longer accepts a callback** – starting with **MapLibre GL v4.0.0** the method returns a **Promise** that resolves with an object `{ data: ImageBitmap }`.  
2. Because the callback is never called, the `addImage('pin', …)` line never runs, so the custom marker image never gets registered.  
3. When the style (or a layer that uses `icon-image: 'pin'`) tries to draw the marker, the image is missing → the icons disappear.

---

## Fix it in two steps

### 1️⃣ Convert the callback-style call to a promise (or `async/await`)

```js
// ❌ Old Mapbox-style code (won’t work in MapLibre ≥ v4)
map.loadImage(url, (err, img) => {
  if (err) throw err;
  map.addImage('pin', img);
});
```

```js
// ✅ New MapLibre-style code
// a) Using async/await (recommended)
async function addPinImage(url) {
  try {
    const { data: img } = await map.loadImage(url);   // ← returns a Promise
    map.addImage('pin', img);
  } catch (err) {
    console.error('Failed to load pin image:', err);
    // handle the error – e.g. fall back to a default icon
  }
}

// Call it after the map’s style is ready (see step 2)
addPinImage('https://example.com/pin.png');
```

```js
// b) Using .then()/.catch()
map.loadImage('https://example.com/pin.png')
   .then(({ data: img }) => map.addImage('pin', img))
   .catch(err => console.error('loadImage error:', err));
```

> **Note:** The resolved object’s property is called `data` (not `image`), and the value is an **`ImageBitmap`** that can be passed directly to `addImage`.

### 2️⃣ Make sure you add the image **after the style is loaded**

If you call `loadImage` before the map’s style has finished loading, `addImage` will throw `Error: Style is not loaded` (or silently fail). The safest place is inside the `load` event or after you’ve called `map.once('styledata', …)`.

```js
map.on('load', () => {
  // The style is now ready – you can safely add custom images
  addPinImage('https://example.com/pin.png');
});
```

If you need the image **before** you add a layer that references it, you can also wait for `styledata`:

```js
map.once('styledata', () => {
  addPinImage('https://example.com/pin.png');
});
```

