### What’s happening?

`map.loadImage` changed in **MapLibre GL v4.0.0** (and later).  
- In Mapbox GL JS the method accepted a **callback** (`(err, image) => …`).  
- In MapLibre GL v4+ the method **returns a Promise** and **ignores any callback argument**.  

Because the callback is never invoked, your `addImage('pin', img)` never runs, so the sprite you later reference in your `Marker` style (`icon-image: 'pin'`) is missing – the markers appear as blank circles (or disappear completely).

### Fix it – use the Promise API

You have three idiomatic ways to handle the returned promise:

| Style | Code example |
|-------|--------------|
| **`async/await`** (most readable) | ```js\nasync function addPin(url) {\n  const { data: img } = await map.loadImage(url);\n  map.addImage('pin', img);\n}\n\naddPin('https://example.com/pin.png');\n``` |
| **`.then()`** chain | ```js\nmap.loadImage('https://example.com/pin.png')\n   .then(({ data }) => map.addImage('pin', data))\n   .catch(err => { console.error(err); });\n``` |
| **`Promise` with `await` inside an IIFE** (if you can’t make the surrounding function async) | ```js\n(async () => {\n  try {\n    const { data } = await map.loadImage('https://example.com/pin.png');\n    map.addImage('pin', data);\n  } catch (e) { console.error(e); }\n})();\n``` |

> **Note:** The resolved value is an object `{ data: HTMLImageElement | ImageBitmap }`. The property is called `data` (not `image`). Pass that `data` to `addImage`.

### Full-example migration

Below is a minimal, self-contained snippet that shows the old Mapbox style and the new MapLibre-compatible version.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <title>MapLibre – loadImage migration</title>
  <link href="https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@^6.0.0/dist/maplibre-gl.css" rel="stylesheet" />
  <style>
    #map { position: absolute; top:0; bottom:0; width:100%; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
<div id="map"></div>

<script type="module">
  import * as maplibregl from 'https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@^6.0.0/dist/maplibre-gl.mjs';

  const map = new maplibregl.Map({
    container: 'map',
    style: 'https://tiles.openfreemap.org/styles/liberty', // any non-mapbox style
    center: [-122.42, 37.78],
    zoom: 12
  });

  // Wait for the style to load before adding sources / images
  map.on('style.load', async () => {
    try {
      // ---- MIGRATED PART ----
      const { data: img } = await map.loadImage(
        'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/maplibre/maplibre-gl-js/main/docs/assets/marker.png'
      );
      // Register the image under the name "pin"
      map.addImage('pin', img);
      // ---- END MIGRATED PART ----

      // Add a source that uses the image
      map.addSource('point', {
        type: 'geojson',
        data: {
          type: 'FeatureCollection',
          features: [{
            type: 'Feature',
            geometry: { type: 'Point', coordinates: [-122.42, 37.78] }
          }]
        }
      });

      // Add a layer that references the image
      map.addLayer({
        id: 'point-layer',
        type: 'symbol',
        source: 'point',
        layout: {
          'icon-image': 'pin',
          'icon-size': 0.5,
          'icon-allow-overlap': true
        }
      });
    } catch (e) {
      console.error('Failed to load marker image:', e);
    }
  });
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

### Checklist after fixing `loadImage`

1. **Replace every `map.loadImage(url, cb)` with a promise version** (search your repo).  
2. **Verify the image name** you pass to `addImage` matches the `icon-image` value in your style/layer definition.  
3. **Check CSS class prefixes** – if you styled the marker with custom CSS that referenced `.mapboxgl-…`, rename those to `.maplibregl-…`. (This does **not** affect the sprite itself, but it can affect control UI.)  
4. **Confirm the style URL** you’re using does not contain any `mapbox://` references (tiles, sprite, glyphs). A missing sprite will also cause icons to disappear.  
5. **Open the browser dev-tools → Network** tab and look for the image request. You should see a `200` response for the PNG/JPEG you’re loading. If you still get a 404/401, the URL is wrong or the server blocks cross-origin requests.

### Why the callback is ignored (more detail)

- In MapLibre GL v4 the signature changed from  
  ```js
  map.loadImage(url: string, callback?: (error: any, image: HTMLImageElement) => void)
  ```  
  to  
  ```js
  map.loadImage(url: string): Promise<{ data: HTMLImageElement | ImageBitmap }>
  ```  
- The implementation now **returns a Promise** and **does not call the supplied callback**. This is why you saw “callback not being called” in the console.

If you have any other Mapbox-style callbacks (e.g., `source.getClusterChildren`, `source.getClusterLeaves`, `source.getClusterExpansionZoom`), they have the same change – they now return promises. Convert them in the same way.

### Quick “search-and-replace” cheat sheet

| Old Mapbox pattern | New MapLibre pattern |
|--------------------|----------------------|
| `map.loadImage(url, (err, img) => { … })` | `const { data: img } = await map.loadImage(url); …` |
| `source.getClusterChildren(clusterId, (err, features) => { … })` | `const { data: features } = await source.getClusterChildren(clusterId); …` |
| `source.getClusterLeaves(clusterId, limit, offset, (err, leaves) => { … })` | `const { data: leaves } = await source.getClusterLeaves(clusterId, limit, offset); …` |
| `source.getClusterExpansionZoom(clusterId, (err, zoom) => { … })` | `const { data: zoom } = await source.getClusterExpansionZoom(clusterId); …` |
| `map.setRTLTextPlugin(url, cb)` | **Remove** – RTL support is built-in from v6.9.0; the call is a no-op. |

### TL;DR

- **`map.loadImage` no longer uses callbacks** – switch to `await map.loadImage(...)` (or `.then`).  
- After the image is loaded, call `map.addImage('pin', img)`.  
- Verify the image name matches the `icon-image` used in your symbol layer.  
- Once the promise-based loading works, your marker icons will appear again.

If you still see blank markers after this change, double-check the **style URL** and **sprite/glyph URLs** for stray `mapbox://` references, and make sure any custom CSS has been renamed from `mapboxgl-` to `maplibregl-`. Feel free to paste the exact snippet that adds the marker if you’d like a more targeted review!

### What’s happening?

