- In Mapbox GL JS the method accepted a *callback* (`(err, image) => …`).  
- In MapLibre GL v4+ the method **returns a `Promise`** and **ignores any callback argument**.  

Because the callback is never invoked, your `addImage('pin', img)` never runs, so the sprite you later reference in your marker style (`icon-image: 'pin'`) is missing – the icons disappear.

### Fix it – use the promise API

You have three idiomatic ways to handle the promise:

| Style | Code |
|-------|------|
| **`async/await`** (most readable) | ```js\nasync function addPinImage(url) {\n  const { data: img } = await map.loadImage(url);\n  map.addImage('pin', img);\n}\naddPinImage('https://example.com/pin.png');\n``` |
| **`.then()`** chain | ```js\nmap.loadImage('https://example.com/pin.png')\n   .then(({ data: img }) => map.addImage('pin', img))\n   .catch(err => { console.error(err); });\n``` |
| **`Promise` with async init** (if you’re inside a `load` handler) | ```js\nmap.on('load', async () => {\n  try {\n    const { data: img } = await map.loadImage('https://example.com/pin.png');\n    map.addImage('pin', img);\n  } catch (e) { console.error(e); }\n});\n``` |

> **Note:** The resolved value is an object `{ data: HTMLImageElement }`. The older callback gave you the raw `HTMLImageElement`; the promise gives you the same image wrapped in `{ data }`.

