### What’s happening?

`map.loadImage` changed in **MapLibre GL v4.0.0** (and later).  
- In Mapbox GL JS the method accepted a **callback** (`(err, image) => …`).  
- In MapLibre GL v4+ the method **returns a `Promise`** and **ignores any callback argument**.  

Because the callback is never invoked, your `addImage('pin', img)` never runs, so the sprite you later reference in your marker style (`icon-image: 'pin'`) is missing – the markers appear as blank circles (or disappear completely).

### Fix it – use the promise API

You have three idiomatic ways to handle the promise:

| Style | Code |
|-------|------|
| **`async/await`** (most readable) | ```js\nasync function addPin(url) {\n  const { data: img } = await map.loadImage(url);\n  map.addImage('pin', img);\n}\naddPin('https://example.com/pin.png');\n``` |
| **`.then()`** chain | ```js\nmap.loadImage('https://example.com/pin.png')\n   .then(({ data: img }) => map.addImage('pin', img))\n   .catch(err => { console.error(err); });\n``` |
| **`Promise` with destructuring** (if you already have a promise) | ```js\nconst imgPromise = map.loadImage('https://example.com/pin.png');\nimgPromise.then(res => map.addImage('pin', res.data)).catch(console.error);\n``` |

> **Important:** The resolved value is an object `{ data: ImageBitmap }`. The image itself is under the `data` key, **not** the raw `ImageBitmap` that the callback used to receive.

### Full-example (including marker creation)

```js
// 1️⃣  Create the map (already done in your app)
const map = new maplibregl.Map({
  container: 'map',
  style: 'https://tiles.openfreemap.org/styles/liberty', // any non-Mapbox style
  center: [-122.42, 37.78],
  zoom: 12
});

// 2️⃣  Load the icon and register it with the style
async function registerPinIcon() {
  try {
    const { data: img } = await map.loadImage(
      'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/maplibre/maplibre-gl-js/main/docs/assets/pin.png'
    );
    // `addImage` will replace an existing image with the same name if you call it again
    map.addImage('pin', img);
  } catch (e) {
    console.error('Failed to load pin image:', e);
  }
}

// 3️⃣  Wait for the style to be ready, then add the source/layer that uses the icon
map.on('style.load', async () => {
  await registerPinIcon();

  // Example GeoJSON source with a single point
  map.addSource('my-points', {
    type: 'geojson',
    data: {
      type: 'FeatureCollection',
      features: [
        {
          type: 'Feature',
          geometry: { type: 'Point', coordinates: [-122.42, 37.78] },
          properties: {}
        }
      ]
    }
  });

  // Layer that uses the newly-added image
  map.addLayer({
    id: 'points',
    type: 'symbol',
    source: 'my-points',
    layout: {
      'icon-image': 'pin',   // <-- matches the name we gave in addImage()
      'icon-size': 0.8
    }
  });
});
```

### Why the marker icons disappear

- **Missing image** – `addImage('pin', img)` never ran, so the style could not resolve `'pin'`.
- **Fallback** – When a symbol layer can’t find the requested image, MapLibre draws a **transparent square** (effectively “no icon”). That’s why you see the markers but without the graphic.

Once the image is successfully added, the icons re-appear.

### Quick checklist for the rest of your migration

| ✅ | Item | What to verify |
|---|------|----------------|
| 1 | **Package & import** | `npm i maplibre-gl` and `import * as maplibregl from 'maplibre-gl';` (or `import {Map} from 'maplibre-gl';`). |
| 2 | **Namespace** | All `mapboxgl` → `maplibregl`. |
| 3 | **Access token** | Remove any `mapboxgl.accessToken = …`. |
| 4 | **Style URL** | No `mapbox://…` URLs. Use an open-source style (e.g., OpenFreeMap, MapTiler, your own). |
| 5 | **Callback → Promise** | `loadImage`, `GeoJSONSource` cluster helpers, `setRTLTextPlugin`, etc. |
| 6 | **CSS class names** | `mapboxgl-` → `maplibregl-` (e.g., `.maplibregl-ctrl`). |
| 7 | **v2-only APIs** | Replace `setFog` → `setSky`, free-camera → `calculateCameraOptionsFromCameraLngLatAltRotation` + `jumpTo/easeTo/flyTo`. |
| 8 | **Plugins** | Verify each plugin: <br>• `@mapbox/mapbox-gl-draw` works after CSS rename (or use `terra-draw`). <br>• `@mapbox/mapbox-gl-geocoder` → `@maplibre/maplibre-gl-geocoder`. <br>• `mapbox-gl-compare` → `@maplibre/maplibre-gl-compare`. |
| 9 | **Tile source** | Ensure every `source` in your style JSON points to a non-Mapbox tile endpoint (e.g., `https://tiles.openfreemap.org/…`). |
|10| **Glyphs / sprites** | If you kept a Mapbox style, replace `glyphs` and `sprite` URLs with ones that actually exist for your new source (or host your own). |

### TL;DR for your specific problem

```js
// Old (Mapbox) – callback is ignored in MapLibre
map.loadImage(url, (err, img) => { … });

/* New (MapLibre) – use the promise */
map.loadImage(url)
   .then(({ data: img }) => map.addImage('pin', img))
   .catch(err => console.error(err));
```

After swapping to the promise version, the image is added, the `'pin'` symbol resolves, and your markers show up again. 🎉

