If you run into any other “missing method” or “blank map” errors, let me know the exact message and the code that triggers it – we can troubleshoot the next piece together.

### What’s happening?

`map.loadImage` changed in **MapLibre GL JS v4.0.0** (and later).  
- In Mapbox GL JS the method accepted a **callback** (`(err, image) => …`).  
- In MapLibre GL JS the **callback signature was removed** – the method now **returns a `Promise`** that resolves with an object `{data: ImageBitmap}` (or rejects with an `Error`).  

Because you are still passing a callback, the promise is created but the callback is ignored, so the image never gets added to the style. Consequently any `addImage('pin', …)` you rely on for custom marker icons fails, and the markers disappear.

---

## Quick fix (ESM / async-await)

```javascript
// -------------------------------------------------
// 1️⃣  Load the image – now returns a Promise
// -------------------------------------------------
async function addPinImage(map, url) {
  try {
    // map.loadImage resolves to { data: ImageBitmap }
    const { data: img } = await map.loadImage(url);
    // -------------------------------------------------
    // 2️⃣  Register the image with the style
    // -------------------------------------------------
    map.addImage('pin', img);
  } catch (err) {
    // Same error handling you had before
    console.error('Failed to load pin image:', err);
    throw err;
  }
}

// -------------------------------------------------
// 3️⃣  Call it after the style is ready
// -------------------------------------------------
map.on('load', () => {
  addPinImage(map, 'https://example.com/pin.png')
    .then(() => {
      // now you can add a layer that uses the image
      map.addLayer({
        id: 'my-pins',
        type: 'symbol',
        source: 'my-geojson',
        layout: {
          'icon-image': 'pin',
          'icon-size': 0.8
        }
      });
    });
});
```

### Or, using `.then()` if you prefer not to make an `async` function

```javascript
map.on('load', () => {
  map.loadImage('https://example.com/pin.png')
    .then(({ data: img }) => {
      map.addImage('pin', img);
      // add your layer here …
    })
    .catch(err => {
      console.error('loadImage error:', err);
    });
});
```

---

## Why the change?

| Mapbox GL JS (≤ v3) | MapLibre GL JS (≥ v4) |
|--------------------|----------------------|
| `map.loadImage(url, callback)` | `map.loadImage(url)` → `Promise<{data: ImageBitmap}>` |
| `GeoJSONSource.getClusterChildren(..., callback)` | `source.getClusterChildren(... )` → `Promise<FeatureCollection>` |
| `source.getClusterLeaves(..., callback)` | `Promise<FeatureCollection>` |
| `source.getClusterExpansionZoom(..., callback)` | `Promise<number>` |
| `map.setRTLTextPlugin(url, callback)` | Returns a `Promise`; from v6.9.0 the plugin is no longer needed for Arabic/Hebrew. |

All of those callbacks were removed to make the API more “modern” and to line up with the native `Promise`-based design of the underlying WebGL worker.

---

## Full migration checklist for your case

1. **Replace every `map.loadImage(..., cb)`** with the promise version (as shown above).  
2. **Check for other removed callbacks** (cluster helpers, `setRTLTextPlugin`, etc.) and convert them to promises.  
3. **Verify CSS class names** – MapLibre uses `maplibregl-` instead of `mapboxgl-`. If you have custom CSS that targets `.mapboxgl-marker` or `.mapboxgl-ctrl`, rename them to `.maplibregl-marker` / `.maplibregl-ctrl`. Missing CSS can also make icons appear invisible.  
4. **Confirm the style URL** – make sure the style you’re using (`style: 'https://tiles.openfreemap.org/styles/liberty'` or your own) includes a `sprite` and `glyphs` that are reachable. If the sprite URL is still a `mapbox://` URL, the icons will not load.  
5. **Re-add the image after the `load` event** (or after any style change that clears the image cache). `map.loadImage` must be called **after** the style is fully loaded; otherwise the image is added to a style that later gets replaced and the image disappears.  

---

## Example: Minimal reproducible snippet

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <title>MapLibre – custom marker</title>
  <link href="https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@^6.0.0/dist/maplibre-gl.css" rel="stylesheet" />
  <style>
    #map { position:absolute; top:0; bottom:0; width:100%; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
<div id="map"></div>

<script type="module">
  import * as maplibregl from 'https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@^6.0.0/dist/maplibre-gl.mjs';

  const map = new maplibregl.Map({
    container: 'map',
    style: 'https://tiles.openfreemap.org/styles/liberty', // any non-Mapbox style
    center: [-122.42, 37.78],
    zoom: 12
  });

  map.on('load', async () => {
    try {
      const { data: img } = await map.loadImage(
        'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/maplibre/maplibre-gl-js/main/docs/assets/marker.png'
      );
      map.addImage('pin', img);

      // Add a dummy source + layer that uses the image
      map.addSource('points', {
        type: 'geojson',
        data: {
          type: 'FeatureCollection',
          features: [{
            type: 'Feature',
            geometry: { type: 'Point', coordinates: [-122.42, 37.78] },
            properties: {}
          }]
        }
      });

      map.addLayer({
        id: 'points-layer',
        type: 'symbol',
        source: 'points',
        layout: {
          'icon-image': 'pin',
          'icon-size': 0.8
        }
      });
    } catch (e) {
      console.error('Could not load marker image', e);
    }
  });
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

Run that in a browser and you’ll see the custom pin appear – proving that the promise-based `loadImage` works.

