## Fix it – use the promise API

### 1️⃣ Simple `async/await` version

```javascript
async function addPinIcon(url) {
  try {
    // loadImage now returns a promise
    const { data: img } = await map.loadImage(url);
    // addImage works the same way
    map.addImage('pin', img);
  } catch (err) {
    console.error('Failed to load pin image:', err);
    // you can re-throw if you want the app to stop
    throw err;
  }
}

// Call it after the map is ready (e.g. in the 'load' event)
map.on('load', () => {
  addPinIcon('https://example.com/pin.png');
});
```

### 2️⃣ `.then()` version (if you don’t want `async`)

```javascript
map.on('load', () => {
  map.loadImage('https://example.com/pin.png')
    .then(({ data: img }) => map.addImage('pin', img))
    .catch(err => {
      console.error('loadImage error:', err);
      // optional: throw err;
    });
});
```

### 3️⃣ Keep the old signature for older MapLibre versions (optional)

If you need to support a **pre-v4** MapLibre build (unlikely unless you’re pinned to an old version), you can detect the return type:

```javascript
function loadPin(url) {
  const result = map.loadImage(url);
  // If a Promise is returned, use it; otherwise fall back to callback style
  if (result && typeof result.then === 'function') {
    result.then(({ data }) => map.addImage('pin', data));
  } else {
    // old callback style – will only run on very old builds
    map.loadImage(url, (err, img) => {
      if (err) throw err;
      map.addImage('pin', img);
    });
  }
}
```

---

## Why the marker icons disappear

1. **Image never added** – the style still contains `icon-image: 'pin'` (or whatever name you used) but the image definition is missing, so the renderer drops the icon.
2. **No fallback** – MapLibre does **not** automatically replace a missing image with a default marker; it just renders nothing.

Once `map.addImage('pin', img)` succeeds, any layer that uses `icon-image: 'pin'` (or a `symbol` layer that references the image) will appear again.

---

## Quick checklist after fixing `loadImage`

| ✅ Check | What to verify |
|--------|----------------|
| **Image added** | Open the browser console and run `map.hasImage('pin')` → should return `true`. |
| **Layer uses the image** | In your style JSON or `addLayer` call, confirm `layout: { "icon-image": "pin" }`. |
| **Style loads after the image** | If you add the image **after** the layer is already on the map, call `map.triggerRepaint()` or simply add the image **before** you add the layer (or call `map.setLayoutProperty(layerId, 'icon-image', 'pin')` after the image is added). |
| **No 401/404** | Verify the URL you pass to `loadImage` is reachable (CORS headers must allow the request). |
| **CSS class names** | If you also see UI elements unstyled, rename any `mapboxgl-` CSS classes to `maplibregl-` (e.g., `.mapboxgl-ctrl` → `.maplibregl-ctrl`). |

---

## Full minimal example (including a marker layer)

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <title>MapLibre – custom pin</title>
  <link href="https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@^6.0.0/dist/maplibre-gl.css" rel="stylesheet" />
  <style>
    #map { position:absolute; top:0; bottom:0; width:100%; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
<div id="map"></div>

<script type="module">
  import * as maplibregl from 'https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@^6.0.0/dist/maplibre-gl.mjs';

  const map = new maplibregl.Map({
    container: 'map',
    style: 'https://tiles.openfreemap.org/styles/liberty', // any non-Mapbox style
    center: [-122.42, 37.78],
    zoom: 12
  });

  map.on('load', async () => {
    // 1️⃣ load the custom icon
    const { data: img } = await map.loadImage(
      'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/maplibre/maplibre-gl-js/main/docs/assets/marker.png'
    );
    map.addImage('pin', img);

    // 2️⃣ add a source + layer that uses the icon
    map.addSource('my-point', {
      type: 'geojson',
      data: {
        type: 'FeatureCollection',
        features: [{
          type: 'Feature',
          geometry: { type: 'Point', coordinates: [-122.42, 37.78] },
          properties: {}
        }]
      }
    });

    map.addLayer({
      id: 'my-point-layer',
      type: 'symbol',
      source: 'my-point',
      layout: {
        'icon-image': 'pin',
        'icon-size': 0.8,
        'icon-allow-overlap': true
      }
    });
  });
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

Run this in a modern browser (MapLibre v6+ requires WebGL 2). You should see the custom pin at the map centre.

---

## TL;DR

* **`map.loadImage` no longer accepts a callback** – it returns a promise.  
* Convert your code to `await map.loadImage(url)` (or `.then`) and then call `map.addImage`.  
* After the image is added, any layer that references it (`icon-image: 'pin'`) will render again.  

Once you make that change, the missing-marker problem disappears, and the rest of your Mapbox-to-MapLibre migration (namespace, CSS, style URL, etc.) can stay as-is. Happy mapping!

### TL;DR  
`map.loadImage` stopped accepting a callback in **MapLibre GL v4.0.0** – it now returns a **Promise**. Because the callback is never invoked, the image never gets added to the style, so any symbols that rely on the `pin` image disappear.

Fix it by using the promise API (or `await`) and then call `map.addImage`.  
If you also use custom CSS classes for the marker element, rename the `mapboxgl-…` prefixes to `maplibregl-…` (but the immediate problem is the `loadImage` change).

---

## 1. Why the callback is ignored

| Library | `loadImage` signature (pre-v4) | `loadImage` signature (v4+) |
|---------|------------------------------|-----------------------------|
| **Mapbox GL JS** (v1-v3) | `map.loadImage(url, (error, image) => …)` | Same (still a callback) |
| **MapLibre GL JS** (v4.0.0-now) | *no longer supported* | `Promise<{data: ImageBitmap | HTMLImageElement}>` |

When you upgraded from `mapbox-gl` → `maplibre-gl`, the method signature changed, so the function you passed is simply ignored. The promise resolves (or rejects) silently, and the image never gets added → your marker icons disappear.

---

## 2. The correct way to load an image in MapLibre

### 2-step promise version (most common)

```js
// style URL must already be set and the map must be loaded
map.on('load', async () => {
  try {
    const { data: img } = await map.loadImage('https://example.com/pin.png');
    // `img` is an ImageBitmap (or HTMLImageElement in older browsers)
    map.addImage('pin', img);
  } catch (err) {
    console.error('Failed to load marker image:', err);
  }
});
```

### Or using `.then()` / `.catch()`

```js
map.on('load', () => {
  map.loadImage('https://example.com/pin.png')
    .then(({ data }) => map.addImage('pin', data))
    .catch(err => console.error('loadImage error:', err));
});
```

### What to keep in mind

| Issue | Fix |
|-------|-----|
| **Calling before the map is ready** | Wrap in `map.on('load', …)` or check `map.isStyleLoaded()` |
| **Using a relative URL that fails CORS** | Ensure the image server sends `Access-Control-Allow-Origin:*` or host the image on the same origin |
| **Adding the same image twice** | `map.hasImage('pin')` → skip or `map.updateImage('pin', img)` |
| **Using a raster sprite instead of `loadImage`** | You can also embed the icon in a sprite sheet and reference it via `icon-image: 'pin'` in the style – no `loadImage` needed |

---

