  <style>
    #map { width: 100%; height: 100vh; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
<div id="map"></div>

<script type="module">
  import * as maplibregl from 'https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@^6.0.0/dist/maplibre-gl.mjs';

  const map = new maplibregl.Map({
    container: 'map',
    style: 'https://tiles.openfreemap.org/styles/liberty', // any non-Mapbox style
    center: [-122.42, 37.78],
    zoom: 12
  });

  map.on('load', async () => {
    try {
      const { data: img } = await map.loadImage(
        'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/maplibre/maplibre-gl-js/main/docs/assets/marker.png'
      );
      map.addImage('pin', img);

      // Add a source + layer that uses the image
      map.addSource('point', {
        type: 'geojson',
        data: {
          type: 'FeatureCollection',
          features: [{
            type: 'Feature',
            geometry: { type: 'Point', coordinates: [-122.42, 37.78] }
          }]
        }
      });

      map.addLayer({
        id: 'point-layer',
        type: 'symbol',
        source: 'point',
        layout: {
          'icon-image': 'pin',
          'icon-size': 0.5,
          'icon-allow-overlap': true
        }
      });
    } catch (e) {
      console.error('❌ image load failed', e);
    }
  });
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

Run this in a modern browser (MapLibre v6+). The marker appears because the image is loaded via the promise API and added to the style before the layer is created.

---

## 4. Quick checklist for “marker icons are gone”

| ✅ Done? | What to verify |
|--------|----------------|
| **1️⃣ `map.loadImage` uses promise** | Replace callback with `await` / `.then()` |
| **2️⃣ Image URL is reachable & CORS-allowed** | Open the URL directly in the browser; check network tab for `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` |
| **3️⃣ `map.addImage` is called *after* the image resolves** | Ensure the `await` line is inside a `map.on('load')` handler (or after `map.isStyleLoaded()`) |
| **4️⃣ Layer references the correct `icon-image` name** | The `layout['icon-image']` must match the name you passed to `addImage` (`'pin'` in the example) |
| **5️⃣ No duplicate `addImage` errors** | If you reload the map or call the code twice, guard with `if (!map.hasImage('pin')) …` |
| **6️⃣ CSS class prefixes** | If you style the marker element manually (e.g., a custom HTML marker), rename any `mapboxgl-…` classes to `maplibregl-…` (not required for the image-based symbol above) |

---

## 5. Bonus: If you *must* keep the old callback style

You can wrap the promise in a tiny helper that mimics the old API, but it’s better to migrate fully:

```js
function loadImageCallback(map, url, cb) {
  map.loadImage(url)
    .then(({ data }) => cb(null, data))
    .catch(err => cb(err));
}

// usage (old style)
loadImageCallback(map, url, (err, img) => {
  if (err) throw err;
  map.addImage('pin', img);
});
```

Only use this as a temporary shim while you refactor the rest of the codebase.

---

## 6. Related migration notes (in case you hit other Mapbox-specific issues)

| Feature | Mapbox → MapLibre change | What to do |
|---------|--------------------------|------------|
| **Namespace** | `mapboxgl` → `maplibregl` | Search-replace all occurrences (including CSS class prefixes) |
| **Access token** | `mapboxgl.accessToken = '…'` | **Remove** – MapLibre does not need a token |
| **Style URL** | `mapbox://styles/...` | Use a non-Mapbox style (e.g., OpenFreeMap, MapTiler, your own style JSON) |
| **`setFog`** | Not available | Use `map.setSky()` + `sky` style layer instead |
| **Free-camera API** | `getFreeCameraOptions` / `setFreeCameraOptions` | Use `calculateCameraOptionsFromCameraLngLatAltRotation` → `jumpTo/easeTo/flyTo` |
| **Callbacks → Promises** | `loadImage`, `GeoJSONSource` cluster methods, `setRTLTextPlugin` | Convert to `await` / `.then()` (see above) |
| **Plugins** | Many Mapbox plugins still work, but some need MapLibre forks (`@maplibre/maplibre-gl-compare`, `@maplibre/maplibre-gl-geocoder`, `@maplibre/maplibre-gl-directions`) | Check each plugin’s README; replace if it still imports `mapbox-gl` |

